Z||000007||theogre||04-03-2001||07:13 PM||||I updated the recall articles a bit today. There are now some notes about what is involved in the V6 coolant hose one.<P>I feel the hose one is hardly worth worrying about but it's something to look at. I wouldn't bother a dealer or GM over that. If you are getting the others done maybe then but certainly not by itself... <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||ArchMagi||04-04-2001||12:35 AM||||was just reading the cave  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>so let me get this stright. for the 87 cyls its pointless to get a lower thermostat or temp fan? casue i was thinking of getting the 180 thermostat from rodney.||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||04-04-2001||07:46 PM||||87-88 4 cyl doesn't use a fan switch. the ECM does that job. you would have to wire the switch into the circuit by adding the connector etc....<P>The 180 thermostat is available anywhere. Rodney has them because some people have been having trouble finding them in stock.<P>It's been my experience that if an 87-88 4 cyl is running hot then you have a leak in the cooling system. Even a tiny leak is trouble. Mine was a pain in the ass until I finally found a pinholed heater core. Now the car rarely goes over 200 even in traffic. It might push up more in really hot weather.<P>I'm working with some people on a diferant ECM chip that will have lower fan set points. This is going to be awhile but it will provide the same result as a switch in the older motors. (The holdup is that we're also looking to fix a couple problems with the OE PROM that cause pinging in allot of 87-88 4's.) The new chip WILL NOT increase HP or anything like that.<P>If you have more questions about the fans please start a new thread.||||reg||1
